# Private local assets.
#
# Open3Dmodel GLB files and every derivative built from them.
#
# Reasons, all of which must hold simultaneously:
#
#   1. The model is offered under CC BY-SA 4.0 as stated by the source project.
#      Redistribution is not intended here: Muscle Atlas is for personal use and
#      is not published, sold, hosted, or shared.
#   2. These files are large. The originals are ~6.5 MB each and derivatives are
#      built from them. Committing them would bloat the repository for no benefit
#      to anyone but the owner.
#   3. They must never enter a build. vite.config.ts copies only from public/,
#      and the 3D loader refuses to run without an explicit opt-in, so a stray
#      copy under public/ is still required for anything to ship.
#
# PROVENANCE.json IS committed deliberately: it records where the files came
# from, their SHA-256 hashes, and which derivative came from which original. That
# record is what makes an untracked binary auditable rather than mysterious.

private/assets/open3dmodel/original/
private/assets/open3dmodel/derived/
private/assets/open3dmodel/*.zip

# Belt and braces: refuse these anywhere in the tree, so an accidental move into
# public/ or src/ is caught rather than shipped.
*.glb
*.gltf
*.blend